# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Background {#background}"
msgstr "Background {#background}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial shows how to use [SQOA Solver, a Qiskit Function by JIJ](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver), to solve a maximum independent set (MIS) problem with more binary variables than the selected QPU has qubits. The basic steps are to load an MIS instance from the [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB)](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB) [\\[1\\]](#references), formulate it in quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) form with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper), submit it to SQOA Solver for execution on an IBM&reg; QPU, and validate the returned solution.\n"
msgstr "Ipinapakita ng tutorial na ito kung paano gamitin ang [SQOA Solver, isang Qiskit Function mula sa JIJ](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver), para lutasin ang isang maximum independent set (MIS) na problema na mas marami ang binary variable kaysa sa bilang ng qubit ng napiling QPU. Ang mga pangunahing hakbang ay: mag-load ng MIS instance mula sa [Quantum Optimization Benchmarking Library (QOBLIB)](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB) [\\[1\\]](#references), buuin ito sa quadratic unconstrained binary optimization (QUBO) form gamit ang [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper), isumite ito sa SQOA Solver para patakbuhin sa isang IBM&reg; QPU, at i-validate ang ibinalik na solusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "The maximum independent set problem {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"
msgstr "Ang maximum independent set na problema {#the-maximum-independent-set-problem}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "An independent set is a subset of nodes in a graph such that no two selected nodes share an edge. A maximum independent set (MIS) is an independent set with the largest possible number of nodes. Applications of MIS include scheduling, resource allocation, and network design.\n"
msgstr "Ang independent set ay isang subset ng mga node sa isang graph kung saan walang dalawang napiling node na may pinagsasaluhang edge. Ang maximum independent set (MIS) ay isang independent set na may pinakamaraming posibleng node. Kabilang sa mga aplikasyon ng MIS ang scheduling, resource allocation, at network design.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "MIS is NP-hard. In an exhaustive search, every additional node doubles the number of subsets to consider, so this approach is impractical even for moderately sized graphs. QOBLIB includes MIS as one of its ten problem classes, so it is a useful benchmark for evaluating quantum optimization workflows on real hardware.\n"
msgstr "Ang MIS ay NP-hard. Sa isang exhaustive search, dumodoble ang bilang ng mga subset na kailangang isaalang-alang sa bawat dagdag na node, kaya hindi praktikal ang pamamaraang ito kahit sa mga graph na katamtaman ang laki. Kasama ang MIS sa sampung klase ng problema ng QOBLIB, kaya isa itong kapaki-pakinabang na benchmark para suriin ang mga quantum optimization workflow sa totoong hardware.\n"

# doq: kept in English by the translator (name or code)
#. type: Title ####
#, no-wrap
msgid "Mathematical formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"
msgstr "Mathematical formulation {#mathematical-formulation}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Given an undirected graph $G = (V, E)$, assign a binary variable $x_v$ to each node $v$:\n"
msgstr "Sa isang undirected graph na $G = (V, E)$, magtalaga ng binary variable na $x_v$ sa bawat node na $v$:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x_v = 1$ if node $v$ is selected.\n"
msgstr "$x_v = 1$ kung napili ang node na $v$.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "$x_v = 0$ otherwise.\n"
msgstr "$x_v = 0$ otherwise.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The [binary linear formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_linear) maximizes the number of selected nodes while preventing both endpoints of any edge from being selected:\n"
msgstr "Ang [binary linear formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_linear) ay ina-maximize ang bilang ng mga napiling node habang pinipigilang mapili ang magkabilang dulo ng alinmang edge:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{x} \\quad & \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} \\quad & x_v + x_w \\leq 1 && \\forall (v,w) \\in E, \\\\\n"
"& x_v \\in \\{0,1\\} && \\forall v \\in V.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\max_{x} \\quad & \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v \\\\\n"
"\\text{subject to} \\quad & x_v + x_w \\leq 1 && \\forall (v,w) \\in E, \\\\\n"
"& x_v \\in \\{0,1\\} && \\forall v \\in V.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The objective counts the selected nodes. Together, the edge constraints ensure that the selected nodes form an independent set.\n"
msgstr "Binibilang ng objective ang mga napiling node. Sama-sama, tinitiyak ng mga edge constraint na bumubuo ng independent set ang mga napiling node.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial uses QOBLIB's [binary unconstrained formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_unconstrained), which replaces the edge constraints with quadratic penalties:\n"
msgstr "Ginagamit ng tutorial na ito ang [binary unconstrained formulation](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/models/binary_unconstrained) ng QOBLIB, na pinapalitan ng mga quadratic penalty ang mga edge constraint:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|V|}} \\quad \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v - 2 \\sum_{(v,w) \\in E} x_v x_w.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\max_{x \\in \\{0,1\\}^{|V|}} \\quad \\sum_{v \\in V} x_v - 2 \\sum_{(v,w) \\in E} x_v x_w.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Whenever both endpoints of an edge are selected, the second term subtracts two from the objective. This penalty makes a conflicting selection less favorable than keeping either endpoint alone. The resulting objective is a QUBO, which is the input format that SQOA Solver accepts.\n"
msgstr "Tuwing napili ang magkabilang dulo ng isang edge, binabawasan ng ikalawang term ang objective ng dalawa. Dahil sa penalty na ito, mas hindi paborable ang magkasalungat na pagpili kaysa sa pagpili ng isa lang sa mga dulo. Ang resultang objective ay isang QUBO, na siyang input format na tinatanggap ng SQOA Solver.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Why use SQOA Solver? {#why-use-sqoa-solver}"
msgstr "Bakit gagamitin ang SQOA Solver? {#why-use-sqoa-solver}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Many quantum optimization approaches assign one qubit to each binary variable, so the capacity of the quantum hardware can directly limit the problem size. SQOA Solver combines several reduction and hybrid-computing techniques to ease this restriction:\n"
msgstr "Maraming quantum optimization approach ang nagtatalaga ng isang qubit sa bawat binary variable, kaya ang kapasidad ng quantum hardware ay direktang maaaring maglimita sa laki ng problema. Pinagsasama ng SQOA Solver ang ilang reduction at hybrid-computing technique para pagaanin ang limitasyong ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**It can tackle problems with more binary variables than the QPU has qubits.** Presolve applies reduction rules that can fix variables and simplify the remaining QUBO while preserving at least one optimal solution. Empirically, presolve can also make the remaining QUBO sparser, which helps the QRAC-based encoding that follows it.\n"
msgstr "**Kaya nitong harapin ang mga problemang mas marami ang binary variable kaysa sa bilang ng qubit ng QPU.** Ang presolve ay naglalapat ng mga reduction rule na kayang mag-fix ng mga variable at pasimplehin ang natitirang QUBO habang pinapanatili ang kahit isang optimal na solusyon. Ayon sa karanasan, maaari ring gawing mas sparse ng presolve ang natitirang QUBO, na nakakatulong sa QRAC-based na encoding na sumusunod dito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "  The solver then uses a QRAC-based encoding derived from Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[3\\]](#references) to represent multiple variables (up to three) with no direct QUBO interaction on the same qubit.\n"
msgstr "  Pagkatapos, gumagamit ang solver ng QRAC-based na encoding na hinango mula sa Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) [\\[3\\]](#references) para katawanin ang maraming variable (hanggang tatlo) na walang direktang QUBO interaction sa iisang qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"  The reductions from presolve and encoding depend on the problem structure. For example, in this tutorial, a 200-variable problem uses only 67 qubits.\n"
"* **It can be less sensitive to hardware noise.** Sample-based quantum diagonalization [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) uses the QPU to sample bitstrings but performs the diagonalization classically. This avoids repeated QPU evaluations for variational parameter updates and can reduce the impact of noise on the optimization workflow.\n"
"* **It automates the workflow from presolve through post-processing.** You provide a correctly formatted QUBO instance and select a backend. SQOA Solver then runs the whole workflow automatically. It applies presolve, maps the classical variables to a relaxed quantum problem, constructs and transpiles the sampling circuits, performs quantum sampling and classical diagonalization, rounds and refines the assignment, and reconstructs and evaluates the classical solution.\n"
msgstr ""
"  Nakadepende sa estruktura ng problema ang mga reduction mula sa presolve at encoding. Halimbawa, sa tutorial na ito, 67 qubit lang ang ginagamit ng isang problemang may 200 variable.\n"
"* **Maaari itong mas hindi sensitibo sa hardware noise.** Ginagamit ng sample-based quantum diagonalization [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references) ang QPU para mag-sample ng mga bitstring pero classical ang paggawa ng diagonalization. Iniiwasan nito ang paulit-ulit na QPU evaluation para sa mga update ng variational parameter at maaaring bawasan ang epekto ng noise sa optimization workflow.\n"
"* **Ina-automate nito ang workflow mula presolve hanggang post-processing.** Magbibigay ka ng wastong naka-format na QUBO instance at pipili ng backend. Pagkatapos, awtomatikong patatakbuhin ng SQOA Solver ang buong workflow. Naglalapat ito ng presolve, imamapa ang mga classical variable sa isang relaxed na quantum problem, bubuuin at ita-transpile ang mga sampling circuit, magsasagawa ng quantum sampling at classical diagonalization, magro-round at magre-refine ng assignment, at muling bubuuin at susuriin ang classical na solusyon.\n"

