# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Understand the SQOA framework {#understand-the-sqoa-framework}"
msgstr "Unawain ang SQOA framework {#understand-the-sqoa-framework}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) [\\[2\\]](#references) combines Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) with sample-based quantum diagonalization:\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng Sampling-based Quantum Optimization Algorithm with Quantum Relaxation (SQOA-QR) [\\[2\\]](#references) ang Quantum Random Access Optimization (QRAO) at sample-based quantum diagonalization:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, no-wrap
msgid "**Quantum relaxation and encoding:** SQOA Solver converts the QUBO to a minimization Ising objective of the form $c + \\sum_i h_i z_i + \\sum_{i<j} J_{ij} z_i z_j$, where $z_i \\in \\{-1, +1\\}$. QRAO [\\[3\\]](#references) then maps each spin variable to a Pauli observable. For the $(3,1)$-QRAC encoding used here, the relaxed Hamiltonian is\n"
msgstr "**Quantum relaxation at encoding:** Kino-convert ng SQOA Solver ang QUBO sa isang minimization Ising objective na may anyong $c + \\sum_i h_i z_i + \\sum_{i<j} J_{ij} z_i z_j$, kung saan $z_i \\in \\{-1, +1\\}$. Pagkatapos, imamapa ng QRAO [\\[3\\]](#references) ang bawat spin variable sa isang Pauli observable. Para sa $(3,1)$-QRAC encoding na ginagamit dito, ang relaxed Hamiltonian ay\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\widetilde{H} = cI + \\sum_i \\sqrt{k_i} h_i P_{f(i)} + \\sum_{i<j} \\sqrt{k_i k_j} J_{ij} P_{f(i)} P_{f(j)},\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\widetilde{H} = cI + \\sum_i \\sqrt{k_i} h_i P_{f(i)} + \\sum_{i<j} \\sqrt{k_i k_j} J_{ij} P_{f(i)} P_{f(j)},\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   where $I$ is the identity operator, $f(i)$ assigns variable $i$ to a qubit and one of $X$, $Y$, or $Z$, and $k_i \\in \\{1,2,3\\}$ is the number of variables mapped to the same qubit as $i$. When both relevant qubits contain three variables, the linear and quadratic scaling factors become $\\sqrt{3}$ and $3$, respectively.\n"
msgstr "   kung saan ang $I$ ay ang identity operator, itinatalaga ng $f(i)$ ang variable na $i$ sa isang qubit at sa isa sa $X$, $Y$, o $Z$, at ang $k_i \\in \\{1,2,3\\}$ ay ang bilang ng mga variable na naka-map sa parehong qubit ng $i$. Kapag may tatlong variable ang parehong kaugnay na qubit, ang mga linear at quadratic scaling factor ay nagiging $\\sqrt{3}$ at $3$, ayon sa pagkakasunod.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Variables that share a qubit are assigned different noncommuting Pauli observables. Variables that interact in the QUBO are kept on different qubits, while variables with no direct QUBO interaction can share a qubit. The reduction in qubit count therefore depends on the structure of the problem.\n"
"2. **Quantum sampling:** A quantum processor samples bitstrings from circuits designed to explore low-energy states of the relaxed Hamiltonian.\n"
"3. **Sample-based diagonalization:** The solver projects the relaxed Hamiltonian onto the subspace spanned by basis states obtained from the sampled bitstrings and diagonalizes the projected Hamiltonian classically [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references). For a fixed set of sampled bitstrings, let $\\mathcal{S}_r$ be the subspace spanned by $r$ distinct basis states, so $\\dim(\\mathcal{S}_r) \\leq r$. Its estimated ground-state energy is:\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ang mga variable na nagbabahagi ng qubit ay itinatalaga ng magkakaibang noncommuting na Pauli observable. Ang mga variable na may interaction sa QUBO ay inilalagay sa magkakaibang qubit, habang ang mga variable na walang direktang QUBO interaction ay maaaring magbahagi ng qubit. Kaya nakadepende sa estruktura ng problema ang pagbawas sa bilang ng qubit.\n"
"2. **Quantum sampling:** Nagsa-sample ang isang quantum processor ng mga bitstring mula sa mga circuit na dinisenyo para tuklasin ang mga low-energy state ng relaxed Hamiltonian.\n"
"3. **Sample-based diagonalization:** Ipinoproject ng solver ang relaxed Hamiltonian sa subspace na sakop ng mga basis state na nakuha mula sa mga na-sample na bitstring at dina-diagonalize ang na-project na Hamiltonian nang classical [\\[4\\]](#references), [\\[5\\]](#references). Para sa isang nakapirming set ng mga na-sample na bitstring, hayaang ang $\\mathcal{S}_r$ ay ang subspace na sakop ng $r$ magkakaibang basis state, kaya $\\dim(\\mathcal{S}_r) \\leq r$. Ang tinatayang ground-state energy nito ay:\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   E_r = \\min_{\\substack{|\\psi\\rangle \\in \\mathcal{S}_r \\\\ \\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle=1}} \\langle\\psi|\\widetilde{H}|\\psi\\rangle, \\qquad \\mathcal{S}_r \\subseteq \\mathcal{S}_{r'} \\Longrightarrow E_{\\mathrm{exact}} \\leq E_{r'} \\leq E_r \\quad (r' \\geq r),\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   E_r = \\min_{\\substack{|\\psi\\rangle \\in \\mathcal{S}_r \\\\ \\langle\\psi|\\psi\\rangle=1}} \\langle\\psi|\\widetilde{H}|\\psi\\rangle, \\qquad \\mathcal{S}_r \\subseteq \\mathcal{S}_{r'} \\Longrightarrow E_{\\mathrm{exact}} \\leq E_{r'} \\leq E_r \\quad (r' \\geq r),\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "   where $E_{\\mathrm{exact}}$ is the ground-state energy of the full relaxed Hamiltonian. Therefore, a larger retained subspace cannot increase the estimated ground-state energy.\n"
msgstr "   kung saan ang $E_{\\mathrm{exact}}$ ay ang ground-state energy ng buong relaxed Hamiltonian. Kaya, hindi maaaring pataasin ng mas malaking pinanatiling subspace ang tinatayang ground-state energy.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   This ordering assumes the same sampling result and concerns the relaxed-Hamiltonian energy before rounding. It does not theoretically guarantee a better returned classical solution. However, in QRAO, a lower-energy state is heuristically expected to provide a better classical solution.\n"
"4. **Rounding:** The relaxed state obtained from the diagonalization is converted into a classical binary assignment.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Ipinapalagay ng pagkakasunod-sunod na ito ang parehong sampling result at tungkol ito sa energy ng relaxed Hamiltonian bago mag-rounding. Hindi nito teoretikal na ginagarantiyahan ang mas mahusay na ibinalik na classical na solusyon. Gayunpaman, sa QRAO, heuristikong inaasahan na ang mas mababang-energy na state ay magbibigay ng mas mahusay na classical na solusyon.\n"
"4. **Rounding:** Ang relaxed state na nakuha mula sa diagonalization ay kino-convert sa isang classical na binary assignment.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver surrounds this framework with classical processing. Before the quantum mapping, presolve applies reduction rules that can fix variables and simplify the remaining QUBO while preserving at least one optimal solution. After the diagonalization and rounding, a classical local search refines the assignment, and OMMX reconstructs and evaluates the complete solution.\n"
msgstr "Binabalutan ng SQOA Solver ang framework na ito ng classical processing. Bago ang quantum mapping, naglalapat ang presolve ng mga reduction rule na kayang mag-fix ng mga variable at pasimplehin ang natitirang QUBO habang pinapanatili ang kahit isang optimal na solusyon. Pagkatapos ng diagonalization at rounding, nire-refine ng isang classical local search ang assignment, at binubuo muli at sinusuri ng OMMX ang kumpletong solusyon.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the instance {#load-the-instance}"
msgstr "I-load ang instance {#load-the-instance}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QOBLIB distributes each MIS instance as a graph in the DIMACS `.gph` format, a line-based format in which the line starting with `p` gives the numbers of nodes and edges and each line starting with `e` defines an edge.\n"
msgstr "Ipinamamahagi ng QOBLIB ang bawat MIS instance bilang graph sa DIMACS `.gph` format, isang line-based na format kung saan ang linyang nagsisimula sa `p` ay nagbibigay ng bilang ng mga node at edge at ang bawat linyang nagsisimula sa `e` ay nagdedefine ng isang edge.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "QOBLIB also publishes an optimal or best-known reference solution for each instance. The following functions download both from the QOBLIB repository. DIMACS labels nodes starting from 1, so the graph is relabeled to start from 0.\n"
msgstr "Naglalathala rin ang QOBLIB ng optimal o best-known na reference solution para sa bawat instance. Dina-download ng mga sumusunod na function ang dalawa mula sa QOBLIB repository. Nagsisimula sa 1 ang pag-label ng DIMACS sa mga node, kaya nire-relabel ang graph para magsimula sa 0.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "If you want to start from your own graph instead, skip the download and formulate the problem from your NetworkX graph in the same way.\n"
msgstr "Kung gusto mong magsimula sa sarili mong graph, laktawan ang download at buuin ang problema mula sa iyong NetworkX graph sa parehong paraan.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You use the objective value of the reference solution later to assess the result from SQOA Solver. This tutorial solves this problem on a device with 156 qubits.\n"
msgstr "Gagamitin mo ang objective value ng reference solution mamaya para suriin ang resulta mula sa SQOA Solver. Nilulutas ng tutorial na ito ang problemang ito sa isang device na may 156 qubit.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the graph. Later, you also use it to verify that the nodes returned by SQOA Solver form an independent set.\n"
msgstr "I-visualize ang graph. Gagamitin mo rin ito mamaya para i-verify na bumubuo ng independent set ang mga node na ibinalik ng SQOA Solver.\n"

# doq: copied, nothing translatable
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/maximum-independent-set-jij-sqoa/extracted-outputs/7c0c796c-0.avif)\n"
msgstr "![Output of the previous code cell](/docs/images/tutorials/maximum-independent-set-jij-sqoa/extracted-outputs/7c0c796c-0.avif)\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Formulate the QUBO {#formulate-the-qubo}"
msgstr "Buuin ang QUBO {#formulate-the-qubo}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Build the binary linear formulation from the Background section as an `OptimizationProblem` with one binary variable per node, an objective that counts the selected nodes, and one constraint per edge. Then convert it with `OptimizationProblemToQubo`.\n"
msgstr "Buuin ang binary linear formulation mula sa seksyong Background bilang isang `OptimizationProblem` na may isang binary variable kada node, isang objective na bumibilang sa mga napiling node, at isang constraint kada edge. Pagkatapos, i-convert ito gamit ang `OptimizationProblemToQubo`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With a penalty weight of 2, the converter replaces each edge constraint with the penalty term $2 x_v x_w$ and turns the maximization into a minimization, so the converted problem is QOBLIB's binary unconstrained formulation with its sign reversed. The QUBO's variable indices are the graph's node labels. The `IndependentSet` application class in `qiskit_addon_opt_mapper.applications` builds the same constrained model with `IndependentSet(G).to_optimization_problem()`.\n"
msgstr "Sa penalty weight na 2, pinapalitan ng converter ang bawat edge constraint ng penalty term na $2 x_v x_w$ at ginagawang minimization ang maximization, kaya ang na-convert na problema ay ang binary unconstrained formulation ng QOBLIB na may baligtad na sign. Ang mga variable index ng QUBO ay ang mga label ng node ng graph. Ang `IndependentSet` application class sa `qiskit_addon_opt_mapper.applications` ay bumubuo ng parehong constrained model gamit ang `IndependentSet(G).to_optimization_problem()`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Finally, convert the QUBO to the dictionary format with `to_problem_dict()`. Because the problem is a binary QUBO, the request in Step 2 declares its variable domain as `\"binary\"`. The function performs presolve, quantum mapping, and circuit construction after submission.\n"
msgstr "Panghuli, i-convert ang QUBO sa dictionary format gamit ang `to_problem_dict()`. Dahil binary QUBO ang problema, idineklara ng request sa Hakbang 2 ang variable domain nito bilang `\"binary\"`. Ginagawa ng function ang presolve, quantum mapping, at circuit construction pagkatapos ng pagsusumite.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 2: Optimize the problem for quantum hardware execution {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"
msgstr "Hakbang 2: I-optimize ang problema para sa pagpapatakbo sa quantum hardware {#step-2-optimize-the-problem-for-quantum-hardware-execution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver performs the quantum mapping and hardware preparation inside the function. It first applies presolve to the QUBO, then maps the remaining variables to a relaxed Hamiltonian by using a QRAC-based encoding.\n"
msgstr "Ginagawa ng SQOA Solver ang quantum mapping at paghahanda ng hardware sa loob ng function. Una nitong inilalapat ang presolve sa QUBO, tapos imamapa ang natitirang mga variable sa isang relaxed Hamiltonian gamit ang QRAC-based na encoding.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For quantum sampling, it constructs circuits based on the relaxed Hamiltonian and transpiles them for the selected backend. The problem-size and qubit reductions from presolve and encoding depend on the problem, so configure the solver without assuming a fixed reduction factor.\n"
msgstr "Para sa quantum sampling, bumubuo ito ng mga circuit batay sa relaxed Hamiltonian at tina-transpile ang mga ito para sa napiling backend. Nakadepende sa problema ang pagbawas sa laki ng problema at bilang ng qubit mula sa presolve at encoding, kaya i-configure ang solver nang hindi ipinapalagay ang nakapirming reduction factor.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Configure the solver inputs {#configure-the-solver-inputs}"
msgstr "I-configure ang mga input ng solver {#configure-the-solver-inputs}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver requires two inputs:\n"
msgstr "Nangangailangan ang SQOA Solver ng dalawang input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`problem`, the dictionary from Step 1.\n"
msgstr "`problem`, ang dictionary mula sa Hakbang 1.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`variable_type`, which is `\"binary\"` for this QUBO.\n"
msgstr "`variable_type`, na `\"binary\"` para sa QUBO na ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "It also accepts two optional inputs:\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap din ito ng dalawang opsyonal na input:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`backend_name` selects the QPU. When it is omitted or `None`, the function selects the least busy operational QPU that is accessible to your instance.\n"
msgstr "Pinipili ng `backend_name` ang QPU. Kapag hindi ito ibinigay o `None`, pinipili ng function ang pinakakaunting abalang operational na QPU na ma-a-access ng iyong instance.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`options` is a dictionary that controls the sampling budget (`shots`), the classical seed (`seed`), session usage (`session`), the classical local search (`postprocessing_level`), and job tags (`job_tags`). If you increase `shots`, the sampling statistics can improve.\n"
msgstr "Ang `options` ay isang dictionary na kumokontrol sa sampling budget (`shots`), sa classical seed (`seed`), sa paggamit ng session (`session`), sa classical local search (`postprocessing_level`), at sa mga job tag (`job_tags`). Kung dadagdagan mo ang `shots`, maaaring gumanda ang sampling statistics.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For all inputs, their default values, and validation rules, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver).\n"
msgstr "Para sa lahat ng input, sa mga default na halaga nito, at sa mga validation rule, tingnan ang [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "This tutorial names the backend explicitly, uses the default values for `shots`, `session`, and `postprocessing_level`, and sets the classical seed. Collect the inputs in a dictionary so that you can pass them to `solver.run()` in Step 3.\n"
msgstr "Tahasang pinangalanan ng tutorial na ito ang backend, ginagamit ang mga default na halaga para sa `shots`, `session`, at `postprocessing_level`, at itinatakda ang classical seed. Ipunin ang mga input sa isang dictionary para maipasa mo ang mga ito sa `solver.run()` sa Hakbang 3.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 3: Execute using primitives {#step-3-execute-using-primitives}"
msgstr "Hakbang 3: Patakbuhin gamit ang mga primitive {#step-3-execute-using-primitives}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Submit the job with the SQOA Solver connection created in Step 1. The function runs the IBM Quantum Sampler primitive on the selected backend, collects the measured bitstrings, and continues with the classical diagonalization and post-processing. You interact with a single function job.\n"
msgstr "Isumite ang job gamit ang koneksyon sa SQOA Solver na ginawa sa Hakbang 1. Pinapatakbo ng function ang IBM Quantum Sampler primitive sa napiling backend, kinokolekta ang mga sinukat na bitstring, at nagpapatuloy sa classical diagonalization at post-processing. Isang function job lang ang kinakausap mo.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "To check the status of the workload, see [Check job status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status). Internally, the function proceeds through mapping, hardware optimization, queue waiting, QPU execution, and post-processing phases.\n"
msgstr "Para tingnan ang status ng workload, tingnan ang [Check job status](/guides/functions-get-started#check-job-status). Sa loob, dumadaan ang function sa mga phase ng mapping, hardware optimization, paghihintay sa queue, QPU execution, at post-processing.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "`job.result()` blocks until the job completes and returns a dictionary with the solution, its objective value and feasibility, and metadata that holds solver information and resource usage. For the full definition of the inputs and outputs, see the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver).\n"
msgstr "Hinaharang ng `job.result()` ang takbo hanggang matapos ang job at nagbabalik ng dictionary na may solusyon, ang objective value at feasibility nito, at metadata na naglalaman ng impormasyon ng solver at resource usage. Para sa buong definisyon ng mga input at output, tingnan ang [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver).\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Step 4: Post-process the result and convert it to a classical format {#step-4-post-process-the-result-and-convert-it-to-a-classical-format}"
msgstr "Hakbang 4: I-post-process ang resulta at i-convert ito sa classical na format {#step-4-post-process-the-result-and-convert-it-to-a-classical-format}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the complete function output, map the returned assignment back to the graph, verify the selected nodes, and visualize the result.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ang kumpletong output ng function, i-map pabalik sa graph ang ibinalik na assignment, i-verify ang mga napiling node, at i-visualize ang resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Inspect the result {#inspect-the-result}"
msgstr "Suriin ang resulta {#inspect-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The result dictionary contains four top-level fields:\n"
msgstr "Ang result dictionary ay may apat na top-level na field:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`solution` is the complete variable assignment, keyed by `x_i`, where _i_ is the variable index (for example, `x_17`). In this tutorial, the variable index is the node label.\n"
msgstr "Ang `solution` ay ang kumpletong variable assignment, na naka-key sa `x_i`, kung saan ang _i_ ay ang variable index (halimbawa, `x_17`). Sa tutorial na ito, ang variable index ay ang label ng node.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`objective_value` is the objective of that assignment evaluated on the submitted dictionary, that is, on the minimization QUBO.\n"
msgstr "Ang `objective_value` ay ang objective ng assignment na iyon na sinuri sa isinumiteng dictionary, ibig sabihin, sa minimization QUBO.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`feasible` refers only to the variable domain, because the dictionary has no constraints.\n"
msgstr "Ang `feasible` ay tumutukoy lang sa variable domain, dahil walang constraint ang dictionary.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '* '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`metadata` contains `solver_info` and `resource_usage`. `solver_info` records the effective `seed` of the run. If the classical local search ran, `solver_info` also records the rounded assignment from before that refinement in `solution_before_postprocessing`.\n"
msgstr "Naglalaman ang `metadata` ng `solver_info` at `resource_usage`. Itinatala ng `solver_info` ang epektibong `seed` ng run. Kung tumakbo ang classical local search, itinatala rin ng `solver_info` ang rounded assignment mula bago ang refinement na iyon sa `solution_before_postprocessing`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Map the solution to the graph {#map-the-solution-to-the-graph}"
msgstr "I-map ang solusyon sa graph {#map-the-solution-to-the-graph}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Collect the returned values in the order of the variable indices, and map them back to the variables of the original problem with `interpret()`. The selected nodes are the variables with the value 1, and `is_feasible()` checks the assignment against the edge constraints of the original problem.\n"
msgstr "Ipunin ang mga ibinalik na halaga ayon sa pagkakasunod-sunod ng mga variable index, at i-map ang mga ito pabalik sa mga variable ng orihinal na problema gamit ang `interpret()`. Ang mga napiling node ay ang mga variable na may halagang 1, at sinusuri ng `is_feasible()` ang assignment laban sa mga edge constraint ng orihinal na problema.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare with the solution before post-processing {#compare-with-the-solution-before-post-processing}"
msgstr "Ihambing sa solusyon bago ang post-processing {#compare-with-the-solution-before-post-processing}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because `postprocessing_level` is `1`, `solver_info` also records the rounded assignment from before the classical local search in `solution_before_postprocessing`. It uses the same keys as `solution`.\n"
msgstr "Dahil `1` ang `postprocessing_level`, itinatala rin ng `solver_info` ang rounded assignment mula bago ang classical local search sa `solution_before_postprocessing`. Pareho ang mga key nito sa `solution`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Evaluate it on the QUBO to see how much the refinement improved the result. Both values are objectives of the submitted minimization QUBO, so a lower value is better. The field is omitted when the local search does not run, for example, when presolve fixes every variable.\n"
msgstr "Suriin ito sa QUBO para makita kung gaano kalaki ang naitulong ng refinement sa resulta. Parehong mga objective ng isinumiteng minimization QUBO ang dalawang halaga, kaya mas maganda ang mas mababang halaga. Hindi isinasama ang field kapag hindi tumakbo ang local search, halimbawa, kapag na-fix ng presolve ang bawat variable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Verify the independence constraint {#verify-the-independence-constraint}"
msgstr "I-verify ang independence constraint {#verify-the-independence-constraint}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Because the QUBO represents adjacency through penalty terms rather than explicit constraints, a heuristic result can still select adjacent nodes. Check the returned nodes directly against the graph. For the comparison and visualization in the following sections, copy the returned set and greedily remove one endpoint of each detected conflict.\n"
msgstr "Dahil kinakatawan ng QUBO ang adjacency sa pamamagitan ng mga penalty term sa halip na tahasang constraint, maaari pa ring mapili ng isang heuristic na resulta ang magkatabing node. Direktang suriin ang mga ibinalik na node laban sa graph. Para sa paghahambing at visualization sa mga susunod na seksyon, kopyahin ang ibinalik na set at greedy na alisin ang isang dulo ng bawat natukoy na conflict.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Compare with the reference solution {#compare-with-the-reference-solution}"
msgstr "Ihambing sa reference solution {#compare-with-the-reference-solution}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In Step 1, you downloaded the objective value of the [QOBLIB reference solution](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/solutions). QOBLIB reference solutions can be optimal or best-known, so compare against the reference objective without assuming that it is always a certified optimum.\n"
msgstr "Sa Hakbang 1, dina-download mo ang objective value ng [QOBLIB reference solution](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset/solutions). Maaaring optimal o best-known ang mga QOBLIB reference solution, kaya ihambing sa reference objective nang hindi ipinapalagay na laging certified optimum ito.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "For this maximization problem, a ratio of 1.0 means that the repaired result matches the reference objective.\n"
msgstr "Para sa maximization na problemang ito, ang ratio na 1.0 ay nangangahulugang tugma ng naayos na resulta ang reference objective.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ###
#, no-wrap
msgid "Visualize the result {#visualize-the-result}"
msgstr "I-visualize ang resulta {#visualize-the-result}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Plot the graph again with the repaired independent set highlighted. No two highlighted nodes share an edge.\n"
msgstr "I-plot muli ang graph na naka-highlight ang naayos na independent set. Walang dalawang naka-highlight na node ang may pinagsasaluhang edge.\n"

