#, no-wrap
msgid "Conclusion {#conclusion}"
msgstr "Konklusyon {#conclusion}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "In this tutorial, you downloaded an MIS instance from QOBLIB, formulated it as a QUBO with `qiskit-addon-opt-mapper`, connected to SQOA Solver, configured and submitted the workload, mapped the returned assignment back to the graph, and checked the selected nodes against the original graph.\n"
msgstr "Sa tutorial na ito, nag-download ka ng MIS instance mula sa QOBLIB, ginawa itong QUBO gamit ang `qiskit-addon-opt-mapper`, kumonekta sa SQOA Solver, kinonfigure at isinumite ang workload, imina-map pabalik sa graph ang ibinalik na assignment, at tiningnan ang mga napiling node laban sa orihinal na graph.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "You also compared the result with the QOBLIB reference solution, examined the contribution of the classical post-processing, and inspected the resource usage of each execution phase.\n"
msgstr "Inihambing mo rin ang resulta sa reference solution ng QOBLIB, sinuri ang kontribusyon ng classical post-processing, at siniyasat ang resource usage ng bawat execution phase.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver combines presolve, QRAO with a QRAC-based encoding, sampling-circuit construction, hardware-aware transpilation, sample-based diagonalization, rounding, and classical refinement. This workflow can map more binary variables than a one-variable-per-qubit encoding would allow. The amount of reduction from presolve and encoding depends on the problem structure, and solution quality depends on the samples obtained.\n"
msgstr "Pinagsasama ng SQOA Solver ang presolve, QRAO na may QRAC-based na encoding, pagbuo ng sampling circuit, hardware-aware na transpilation, sample-based na diagonalization, rounding, at classical refinement. Kaya ng workflow na ito na mag-map ng mas maraming binary variable kaysa sa papayagan ng one-variable-per-qubit na encoding. Ang laki ng pagbawas mula sa presolve at encoding ay nakadepende sa istruktura ng problema, at ang kalidad ng solusyon ay nakadepende sa nakuhang mga sample.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "The `shots` and `postprocessing_level` settings control the quantum sampling budget and the classical refinement, respectively, without changing the submission workflow.\n"
msgstr "Kinokontrol ng mga setting na `shots` at `postprocessing_level` ang quantum sampling budget at ang classical refinement, ayon sa pagkakasunod, nang hindi binabago ang submission workflow.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Appendix: Submit the problem as an OMMX instance {#appendix-submit-the-problem-as-an-ommx-instance}"
msgstr "Appendix: Isumite ang problema bilang OMMX instance {#appendix-submit-the-problem-as-an-ommx-instance}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver also accepts an `ommx.v1.Instance` from the [OMMX](https://jij-inc.github.io/ommx/en/introduction.html) SDK. The [OMMX Quantum Benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/) package distributes the QOBLIB problems as OMMX instances together with their reference solutions, so you can load the same QUBO without formulating it yourself.\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap din ang SQOA Solver ng `ommx.v1.Instance` mula sa [OMMX](https://jij-inc.github.io/ommx/en/introduction.html) SDK. Ang package na [OMMX Quantum Benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/) ay nagdi-distribute ng mga problema ng QOBLIB bilang OMMX instance kasama ang kanilang mga reference solution, kaya mailo-load mo ang parehong QUBO nang hindi mo ito kailangang i-formulate.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "With an OMMX input, `objective_value` is evaluated in the sense of the instance, and the result also contains the canonical `ommx.v1.Solution`. Install the package, which also installs the OMMX SDK:\n"
msgstr "Sa OMMX input, ang `objective_value` ay sinusuri ayon sa kahulugan ng instance, at naglalaman din ang resulta ng canonical na `ommx.v1.Solution`. I-install ang package, na nag-i-install din ng OMMX SDK:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Load the `binary_unconstrained` model of the same instance. The dataset loader prints progress messages, so the code captures them to keep the output compact.\n"
msgstr "I-load ang `binary_unconstrained` model ng parehong instance. Nagpi-print ng mga progress message ang dataset loader, kaya kinukuha ng code ang mga ito para manatiling compact ang output.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "SQOA Solver receives an OMMX instance as a standard padded Base64 string and returns the canonical solution in the same format. Define two helper functions for this conversion:\n"
msgstr "Tumatanggap ang SQOA Solver ng OMMX instance bilang standard padded Base64 string at ibinabalik ang canonical solution sa parehong format. Tumukoy ng dalawang helper function para sa conversion na ito:\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`to_problem_payload()` serializes an `ommx.v1.Instance` into the string that you pass as `problem`.\n"
msgstr "Sina-serialize ng `to_problem_payload()` ang isang `ommx.v1.Instance` tungo sa string na ipapasa mo bilang `problem`.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Bullet: '- '
#, no-wrap
msgid "`to_ommx_solution()` decodes the canonical `ommx.v1.Solution` from the result.\n"
msgstr "Dine-decode ng `to_ommx_solution()` ang canonical na `ommx.v1.Solution` mula sa resulta.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid "Submit the instance with the same inputs as before, replacing only `problem`. Then decode the canonical solution and read the selected nodes by variable name.\n"
msgstr "Isumite ang instance gamit ang parehong mga input tulad ng dati, `problem` lang ang papalitan. Pagkatapos, i-decode ang canonical solution at basahin ang mga napiling node ayon sa pangalan ng variable.\n"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-12
#. type: Title ##
#, no-wrap
msgid "Next steps {#next-steps}"
msgstr "Mga susunod na hakbang {#next-steps}"

# doq: translated after an English change 2026-11-13
#. type: Plain text
#, no-wrap
msgid ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Recommendations\">\n"
"* Apply the workflow to your own QUBO problems. Build an `OptimizationProblem` as shown in the [SQOA Solver guide](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver). The steps for conversion and submission remain the same, but adapt the validation to the structure of your problem.\n"
"* Submit the problem as an OMMX instance, as shown in the [appendix](#appendix-submit-the-problem-as-an-ommx-instance). See the [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver) for the accepted problem formats and the returned fields.\n"
"* Explore other independent-set instances in the [QOBLIB repository](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) or through [OMMX Quantum Benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/).\n"
"* Learn more about modeling with [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper) or [JijModeling](https://jij-inc-jijmodeling-tutorials-en.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/latest/introduction.html) and exchanging problems with [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"
msgstr ""
"<Admonition type=\"tip\" title=\"Mga Rekomendasyon\">\n"
"* Ilapat ang workflow sa sarili mong mga QUBO problem. Bumuo ng `OptimizationProblem` tulad ng ipinapakita sa [SQOA Solver guide](/guides/jij-sqoa-solver). Pareho pa rin ang mga hakbang para sa conversion at pagsumite, ngunit iangkop ang validation sa istruktura ng iyong problema.\n"
"* Isumite ang problema bilang OMMX instance, tulad ng ipinapakita sa [appendix](#appendix-submit-the-problem-as-an-ommx-instance). Tingnan ang [API reference](https://docs.quantum.ibm.com/api/functions/jij-sqoa-solver) para sa mga tinatanggap na format ng problema at sa mga ibinabalik na field.\n"
"* Mag-explore ng iba pang independent-set instance sa [QOBLIB repository](https://github.com/ZIB-AOPT/QOBLIB/tree/main/07-independentset) o sa pamamagitan ng [OMMX Quantum Benchmarks](https://jij-inc.github.io/OmmxQuantumBenchmarks/).\n"
"* Matuto pa tungkol sa pagmomodelo gamit ang [qiskit-addon-opt-mapper](https://github.com/Qiskit/qiskit-opt-mapper) o [JijModeling](https://jij-inc-jijmodeling-tutorials-en.readthedocs-hosted.com/en/latest/introduction.html) at sa pagpapalitan ng mga problema gamit ang [OMMX](https://ommx-en-book.readthedocs.io/en/latest/).\n"
"</Admonition>\n"

